# API contracts

- `internal/apitypes` is the contract: wire types only, standard library only, doc comments on everything (they are copied into the TypeScript). `frontend/src/api/types.gen.ts` is generated from it by `scripts/gen-types.sh` (tygo, version pinned in the script, config in `tygo.yaml`); CI fails if it is stale. Never edit the generated file.
- Enum-like constants must be named `<TypeName><Value>` (e.g. `ErrorCodeNotFound`, `JobStatusQueued`) so tygo emits TypeScript unions.
- Pointer fields: with `omitempty` they are optional request fields; without it they are nullable response fields and need `tstype:"T | null,required"` (`TestNullableFieldsAreTyped` enforces this).
- Conventions (see `docs/API.md`): resources returned bare, collections as `{items: []}` and never null, RFC 3339 UTC timestamps, one error envelope `{error:{code,message,request_id,field?}}` with stable snake_case `ErrorCode`s. A new error code goes here, in the API doc table, and into the regenerated file.
- `Project.allow_custom_dockerfile` is a boolean with default false. Only an admin may set it in PATCH. A referenced static file requires an admin session for replacement or a deletion attempt. See API.md for the 403 and 409 cases.
- `Project.static_addons`, `Build.server_ids`, `Image.build_ids`/`server_ids` and `BackupList.items` are never null (`[]`).
- `Inspector`, `InspectorTarget`, `InspectorSession` and the server's `inspector`/`inspector_active` follow the doc comments in `inspector.go` and `servers.go`; the hub's secrets and anything a game writes (target labels, errors) never reach them.
- No type may carry a stored secret (password hash, token hash, Git credential, env value, admin token, private key) back to clients. Write-only secret inputs (`ProjectAuth`, server env, `UpdateGameCertificateRequest.PrivateKeyPEM`) never appear in responses. Everything a game reports (`ServerRuntime`) is untrusted. Sanitize it and discard strings containing the admin token before they reach a wire type. Game containers can read their mounted certificate key and can print it into a game log, which is game-supplied text. The server and installation certificate fields are nullable and describe the applicable pair as specified in the API contract.
- Every v1 route is implemented; `not_implemented` (501) is reserved for a route documented before it is built. When `docs/API.md` and a handler disagree, the handler wins and the doc is fixed (state exact codes, fields and bounds, e.g. `tail`, `replace`, import errors).
